From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: hardware flow offload (IPQ95xx/IPQ53xx PPE)

Squashed port of the GL.iNet Flint 3 (IPQ5332) PPE flowtable offload
series (perceival/openwrt-flint3 branch flint3-be9300, patches 0411-0446,
31 commits, all by Kamil Bienkiewicz) onto the IPQ9574 qcom-ppe driver,
rebased with three context fixes for our tree:

- ppe.h: mutex include hunk context adapted (no device.h/of.h in our base)
- ppe.c: probe ordering (ppe_offload_init/_destroy) hand-applied
- ppe_flow.c: dev_warn_once -> pr_warn_once (not in 6.18)

What it implements: PPE flow/host/nexthop/pub-IP table indirect ops,
IPv4 5-tuple flow entry encoding, IPv4 SNAT offload driven by the
netfilter flowtable (flow_offloading_hw, mtk_ppe model), per-flow
counters, VLAN push, DSA-tag aliasing, TC_SETUP_FT/block registration.
Register map: APPE IPE_L3 (matches OSS qca-ssdk hppe_flow_reg.h/
hppe_ip_reg.h "#if defined(APPE)" branches, ISC licensed).

Verified: applies cleanly on qualcommbe 6.18.52 (openwrt main patch set)
and the module builds (aarch64 gcc 14.4) - runtime validation on
TP-Link Archer BE800 pending.

Original per-commit series preserved in research/ppe-offload/flint3-upstream-series/.
Upstream-Status: inappropriate / WIP port - see docs/be800-ppe-offload.md
Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
[BE800 port]
Signed-off-by: Benoit Masson <yahoo@perenite.com>
